hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"314","On the authority of Ali ibn Hajar al-Saadi, on the authority of Ismail ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Al-Alaa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqoub, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The five daily prayers, and Friday prayers after Friday prayers, are expiations for what is between them, as long as the major sins are not overlooked.”"
"315","I am Yunus bin Abdul Ala Al-Sadafi, I am Ibn Wahb, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Ibn Abi Hilal told him that Naim bin Al-Mujmar told him that Suhayb, the client of the Atawaris, told him that he heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri tell about The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on the pulpit, then said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul,” three times, then he remained silent, and each of us fell down. He cried sadly at the right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said: “There is no servant who performs the five daily prayers and fasts Ramadan. And he avoids the seven great sins, except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, to the point that they will clap. Then he recited: If you avoid the great sins “Whatever you are forbidden, We will remit from you your evil deeds.” Surat An-Nisa, Verse 31."
